# ggen working-tree artifact pins
# Format: <kind> <sha256> <bytes> <name>
#
# Contract (transcribed from graphlaw/registry/ARTIFACTS.sha256):
#   Regenerate after any src/ change; the pin is not a live check -- a stale
#   pin is a FINDING to be adjudicated, not a guard that fires by itself.
#
# Regeneration commands (run from the repo root, record observed date):
#   binary pin:
#     cargo build --locked --release -p ggen-cli-lib --bin ggen
#     shasum -a 256 target/release/ggen
#   book/docs manifest pin:
#     python3 book/scripts/assemble_book.py
#     python3 book/scripts/build_static_html.py
#     python3 book/scripts/generate_manifest.py
#     shasum -a 256 book/dist/MANIFEST.sha256
#
# This file is freeze_policy: checksum -- a hand-edit is refused by the next
# sync (manual edit detected) rather than silently clobbered; regenerate via
# the commands above, then delete this file to let the sync re-project it.
# Append observed pin lines below in the <kind> <sha256> <bytes> <name> form.

